    "_about": "THE ALPINE IBEX (Capra ibex; 2026-11-08, generator tools/creaturegen/ungulates/gen.py, on the deer frame): a billy of about 0.94 m at the shoulder -- a stocky wild goat: the chamois' sculpt (its sure-footed cloven legs, its body and its head) scaled 1.18, the trunk and neck deeper and broader (a deeper chest, a thicker neck and shoulders, the belly blended in smooth), the head 1.1 again, its face mask taken off. The HORNS (`horn`s, mirrored): great scimitars from the brow, close together, rising and sweeping back in one arc of about 0.95 m, spreading a little, with the KNOBS across their fronts -- a ridge every 5 cm (the radius up 20%, the section wider), shallow troughs between. A short pointed BEARD (a `fin` tuft under the chin). A fairly even grey-brown with no flank stripe: a slightly darker line down the back, a darker brown chest front and legs, a paler belly, every edge gradual (paints and `kc` ~7 cm); a goat ear about 12 cm long (the chamois' cupped `fin` leaf), set out sideways and back, a little up, its hollow forward and down, so its body-coloured outside reads in profile, body-coloured with a paler inside. Lives on the crags (index.html cragRange, as the chamois)."
  },
